plurx-player (0.3.1+lp7.387.0.mpv0.41.0+git20261026.e59d90c-1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * The player window no longer opens black and closes on an NVIDIA GPU.
    The NVIDIA driver (615) gives an sRGB swapchain a Wayland colour
    surface of its own and keeps it after that swapchain is gone, so mpv's
    request for the window's colour surface, made when the HDR video
    arrives, ended the Wayland connection. Wayland swapchains now start
    pass-through, so mpv is the only one that describes the window.
  * Opened from Chrome, the launcher finds the desktop's display even when
    xdg-desktop-portal started it without one: it takes WAYLAND_DISPLAY,
    DISPLAY, XAUTHORITY, XDG_SESSION_TYPE and XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP from the
    user session, and nothing else.
  * A title with video that mpv cannot open a window for fails with a
    dialog instead of playing its audio with no picture.
  * Every control exchange carries the player's capabilities, as the
    playback control protocol requires, and the server knows a Linux
    client (it answered 400 and then 409 before).
  * Profile 7 titles arrive with both layers once the server is on this
    release's plurx: a copy used to narrow every dual-layer source to its
    HDR10 base, even for a client that names Profile 7.

 -- plurx contributors <noreply@plurx.invalid>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000

plurx-player (0.3.0+lp7.387.0.mpv0.41.0+git20261026.e59d90c-1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Profile 7 FEL titles play with their full enhancement layer, composed
    on the laptop's GPU before the closed-form mapping: plurx sends the
    original stream (the caps claim Dolby Vision profile 7), so nothing is
    re-encoded.
  * Private libplacebo 7.387.0 and mpv master e59d90c84 (2026-10-26),
    the first with FEL composition, plus a split of the enhancement layer
    that works with Ubuntu's FFmpeg 8.1, and no zero MaxCLL/MaxFALL in the
    Wayland image description.
  * dv-brightness=relative|absolute (mpv.conf): follow the desktop's HDR
    brightness setting (default), or map for the panel's real luminance.
  * libplacebo is linked into mpv statically, its symbols renamed
    plurx_pl_* and hidden, because the system FFmpeg's libavfilter loads
    the system libplacebo
    (another major version) into the same process and a private shared
    libplacebo would take over its unversioned pl_* calls.
  * Closed-form equations: tools/dv_processing dm 193c40343ebf (sha256 of
    dm_closed_form.h then dv_dm.h, first 12 hex digits). CM v2.9 evaluates
    its output lattice once per frame, and each method's passes are their
    own shaders: a 4K CM v2.9 frame's mapping takes 19 ms instead of 34 ms
    on an Intel Arc iGPU.

 -- plurx contributors <noreply@plurx.invalid>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

plurx-player (0.2.0+lp7.360.1.mpv0.41.0-1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * mpv maps Dolby Vision profile 5 and 8 with plurx's closed-form CM v4.0
    and CM v2.9 display management (tools/dv_processing/dv_dm.h, the
    server's own code), for the compositor's preferred luminance and the
    largest named gamut inside the panel's primaries, and logs one
    "plurx mapper:" line per configuration.
  * Build-Depends on libdovi-dev for the RPU parser; its C API header is
    the pinned copy in packaging/libdovi.

 -- plurx contributors <noreply@plurx.invalid>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

plurx-player (0.1.1+lp7.360.1.mpv0.41.0-1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Launcher (milestone M4): redeem, decide, play in mpv, heartbeat,
    progress, seek re-creation, teardown.
  * Package a private libplacebo 7.360.1 and mpv 0.41.0, the versions
    Ubuntu 26.10 ships, under /usr/lib/plurx-player (milestone M5
    packaging). mpv is linked with DT_RPATH $ORIGIN/../lib and leaves no
    build path behind.
  * Build from a Debian source package (3.0 (quilt)): the launcher is the
    main orig tarball and the pinned libplacebo and mpv tarballs are its
    component orig tarballs, so the corresponding source of the GPL mpv and
    LGPL libplacebo binaries is published beside the .deb.
  * Apply the patch series from packaging/patches/<name>/series, exactly.
    It is empty until the Dolby Vision closed-form patches land.
  * Run mpv with plurx Player's own --config-dir
    ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/plurx-player/mpv), never the general ~/.config/mpv,
    with --ytdl=no, and without LD_LIBRARY_PATH, LD_PRELOAD or LD_AUDIT.
  * Byte-compile the launcher with dh_python3, whose prerm removes every
    .pyc, so removal leaves nothing behind.
  * Add the plurx-player(1) manual page. Recommend desktop-file-utils and a
    Vulkan driver; record the statically linked glslang and SPIRV-Tools in
    Built-Using and debian/copyright.

 -- plurx maintainers <noreply@plurx.invalid>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
